ules adsorbed to mica flakes. <source>J. Mol. Biol.</source> <volume>169</volume>:<fpage>155</fpage>&#x02013;195.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6684695</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><citation citation-type="journal">Heuser, J.E. <year>1989</year>a. Protocol for 3-D visualization of molecules on mica via the quick-freeze, deep-etch technique. <source>J. Electron Microsc. Tech.</source> <volume>13</volume>:<fpage>244</fpage>&#x02013;263.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2585121</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><citation citation-type="journal">Heuser, J.E. <year>1989</year>b. Effects of cytoplasmic acidification on clathrin lattice morphology. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>108</volume>:<fpage>401</fpage>&#x02013;411.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2563729</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><citation citation-type="journal">Heuser, J.E. <year>2000</year>a. Membrane traffic in anaglyph stereo. <source>Traffic.</source> <volume>1</volume>:<fpage>35</fpage>&#x02013;37.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11208057</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib17"><citation citation-type="journal">Heuser, J.E. <year>2000</year>b. The production of &#x02018;cell cortices&#x02019; for light and electron microscopy: follow the middle road. <source>Traffic.</source> <volume>1</volume>:<fpage>545</fpage>&#x02013;552.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11208142</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib18"><citation citation-type="journal">Heuser, J.E. <year>2000</year>c. How to convert a traditional electron microscopy laboratory to digital imaging. <source>Traffic</source>. <volume>1</volume>:<fpage>614</fpage>&#x02013;621.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11208149</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><citation citation-type="journal">Hisanaga S., H. Murofushi, K. Okuhara, R. Sato, Y. Masuda, H. Sakai, and N. Hirokawa. <year>1989</year>. The molecular structure of adrenal medulla kinesin. <source>Cell Motil. Cytoskeleton.</source> <volume>12</volume>:<fpage>264</fpage>&#x02013;272.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2497994</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><citation citation-type="journal">Holtzman, D.A., S. Yang, and D.G. Drubin. <year>1993</year>. Synthetic-lethal interactions identify two novel genes, SLA1 and SLA2, that control membrane cytoskeleton assembly in <italic>Saccharomyces cerevisiae</italic>. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>122</volume>:<fpage>635</fpage>&#x02013;644.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8335689</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><citation citation-type="journal">Itoh, T., S. Koshiba, T. Kigawa, A. Kikuchi, S. Yokoyama, and T. Takenawa. <year>2001</year>. Role of the ENTH domain in phosphatidylinositol-4,5-bisphosphate binding and endocytosis. <source>Science.</source> <volume>291</volume>:<fpage>1047</fpage>&#x02013;1051.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11161217</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib22"><citation citation-type="journal">Jarousse, N., and R.B. Kelly. <year>2001</year>. Endocytic mechanism in synapses. <source>Curr. Opin. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>13</volume>:<fpage>461</fpage>&#x02013;469.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11454453</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib23"><citation citation-type="journal">Kalchman, M.A., H.B. Koide, K. McCutcheon, R.K. Graham, K. Nichol, K. Nishiyama, P. Kazemi-Esfarjani, F.C. Lynn, C. Wellington, M. Metzler et al. <year>1997</year>. HIP1, a human homologue of <italic>S. cerevisiae</italic> Sla2p, interacts with membrane-associated huntingtin in the brain. <source>Nat. Genet.</source> <volume>16</volume>:<fpage>44</fpage>&#x02013;53.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9140394</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib24"><citation citation-type="journal">Kay, B.K., M. Yamabhai, B. Wendland, and S.D. Emr. <year>1999</year>. Identification of a novel domain shared by putative components of the endocytic and cytoskeletal machinery. <source>Protein Sci.</source> <volume>8</volume>:<fpage>435</fpage>&#x02013;438.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10048338</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib25"><citation citatio